{"content":[{"c":["HAGRITE"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Arabian tribe descended from Hagar, Abraham’s concubine. Being nomads, the Hagrites roamed the desert east of Gilead. Relations between Israel and the Hagrites were usually hostile. During Saul’s reign, Reuben’s tribe fought them and were defeated (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.5.10","r":"1Chr.5.10","rawR":"1Chr.5.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.5.10","value":"1Chr.5.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 5:10"},"). Later, however, with the help of Gad and the half-tribe of Manasseh, Reuben was able to take their land and hold it until the exile (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.5.19-20","r":"1Chr.5.19-20","rawR":"1Chr.5.19-20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.5.19-20","value":"1Chr.5.19-20"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 5:19-20"},"). In the light of that hostility, it is easy to understand Asaph’s prayer against them in ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.83.6","r":"Ps.83.6","rawR":"Ps.83.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.83.6","value":"Ps.83.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Psalm 83:6"},". David, on the other hand, made a Hagrite, Jaziz, the steward of all his flocks (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.27.31","r":"1Chr.27.31","rawR":"1Chr.27.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.27.31","value":"1Chr.27.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 27:31"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Hagrite","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Chr 5:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.5.10","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.5.10","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.5.10"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 5:19-20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.5.19-20","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.5.19-20","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.5.19-20"},{"anchorText":"Psalm 83:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.83.6","rawQueryValue":"Ps.83.6","sourceRefExact":"Ps.83.6"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 27:31","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.27.31","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.27.31","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.27.31"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"ec34dc5cec414c9b4a09cda5fae17459407a82e30fb91d23a23f9b6e5ca2ff18","sourceItemName":"Hagrite","sourceItemOrder":41,"sourceMember":"Articles/H.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Hagrite","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Hagrite","title":"Hagrite","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}